knext bundled fix for vinext 1.1.0 (dist output)
Upstream: https://github.com/cloudflare/vinext/pull/3760 (issue https://github.com/cloudflare/vinext/issues/3757)
What it fixes: `import data from "../data" with { type: "json" }` on a file with no `.json`
extension failed to build with a parse error, because Vite and Rolldown pick the JSON loader by
extension only. webpack and Turbopack honour the attribute (Next.js e2e `import-attributes`,
`import-assertion`). A new pre-transform plugin (dist/plugins/json-import-attributes.js) appends a
`?lang.json` query to such specifiers (static, re-export and dynamic imports), which routes them
through Vite's JSON plugin.
Retire: delete this file (and its manifest entry) when the pinned vinext is >= the first
release that includes cloudflare/vinext#3760.
Ported by hand from the upstream src change to the published 1.1.0 dist files.
Applied by `knext vinext-patches` (runs from the app's postinstall and before `knext build`).

